      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To observe the changes in mitogen-activated protein kinase (MAPK) activity and gene expression after coronary artery balloon injury in rat."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Forty Wistar rats were randomly divided into control group (without coronary artery balloon injury), and 3, 7 and 14 days after coronary artery balloon injury groups (n=10, respectively). The activity of MAPK was measured by biochemical method and the gene expression was examined by reverse transcription-polymerase chain reaction (RT-PCR)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "MAPK activity and gene expression of MAPK in the coronary artery balloon injury in rat after 3, 7 and 14 days were significantly higher than that of normal control, especially 3 days after injury [MAPK activity: (17.32+/-2.17) pmol x mg(-1) x min(-1);MAPK protein: ERK1 was 194.7+/-8.6, ERK2 was 175.8+/-7.9; MAPK gene expression: ERK1 was 1.15+/-0.21, ERK2 was 1.13+/-0.14 ]."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The increase activity and mRNA of MAPK may be involved in the restenosis process after coronary balloon injury."
        }
      ]},
